<title>GREECE: BANK/GREECE HAS LOWEST P/E ON ATHENS BOURSE.</title>
<headline>BANK/GREECE HAS LOWEST P/E ON ATHENS BOURSE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Greece shares</p>
<p>were trading at 1.9 times estimated 1997 pre-tax earnings, the</p>
<p>lowest price earnings ratio (P/E) among all Athens bourse</p>
<p>listings, said Investment Analysis, a financial services</p>
<p>company.</p>
<p>It was followed by Atemke and ETMA </p>
<p>The firms with the lowest estimated 97 pretax P/E multiples</p>
<p>follow:</p>
<p>    1) Bank of Greece	    1.9</p>
<p>    2) Atemke			2.4</p>
<p>    3) Etma			  3.2</p>
<p>    4) Hellatex		    3.3</p>
<p>    5) Diekat			3.5</p>
<p>    6) Parnassos		   3.6</p>
<p>    7) Fanco			  3.7</p>
<p>    8) Mesochoritis		3.9</p>
<p>    9) Papaellinas		  3.9</p>
<p>   10) Zamba			  3.9</p>
<p>   11) European Tech	     4.0</p>
<p>   12) Ekter			 4.2</p>
<p>   13) Ergas			 4.3</p>
<p>   14) Xylemporia		   4.4</p>
<p>   15  Tasoglou		     4.4</p>
<p>Calculations have been based on closing prices of June 7.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
